@*
    THE BRAIN, STILL IMPROVING ITSELF.

    After a model is on the phone it is "ready" — but the engine then spends hours of the
    phone's idle, charging time optimising it into an index (IndexingQueue), and until this
    nothing on a screen said so past a one-line caption. This shows how far that has got, as
    a share, and — when the phone is off its charger — that it carries on once it is back on.

    NO COUNTDOWN, AND THAT IS THE HONEST SHAPE OF IT. The optimise is built from the model
    already here, a unit at a time, only while the phone is idle and on the charger — so it
    has no byte rate and no time left to give. A bar and a share is the whole truth; a ticking
    estimate would be a guess, which is the one thing a progress bar must never be.

    SILENT WHEN THERE IS NOTHING TO OPTIMISE. Null from IndexingAsync renders no markup, so
    this can sit on Home and Setup without becoming furniture — the same contract as
    PairingNotice.
*@
@inject ISetup Setup
@implements IDisposable

@if (_index is { } ix)
{
    <section class="optimising" aria-labelledby="optimising-title">
        <div class="optimising-title" id="optimising-title">Optimising the brain</div>
        <div class="optimising-bar"><span style="width:@($"{Math.Clamp(ix.Percent, 0, 100)}%")"></span></div>
        <div class="optimising-line">@ix.Line</div>
        @if (ix.OnHold && ix.HoldReason is { Length: > 0 })
        {
            <div class="optimising-hold">@ix.HoldReason</div>
        }
    </section>
}

@code {
    private IndexProgress? _index;
    private bool _gone;

    // ADAPTIVE, NOT A FIXED TICK. Nothing is optimising most of the time, so when there is
    // nothing to show the link is asked only every twenty seconds — one cheap verb, the same
    // floor Home's own idle poll uses. While it IS building the bar should feel live, so the
    // read quickens; either way it is one poll, stopped the moment the component goes.
    private static readonly TimeSpan WhenBuilding = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(4);
    private static readonly TimeSpan WhenIdle = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(20);

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        await ReadAsync();
        _ = WatchAsync();
    }

    private async Task WatchAsync()
    {
        while (!_gone)
        {
            try { await Task.Delay(_index is null ? WhenIdle : WhenBuilding); } catch { return; }
            if (_gone) return;
            await ReadAsync();
        }
    }

    private async Task ReadAsync()
    {
        IndexProgress? fresh;
        try { fresh = await Setup.IndexingAsync(); }
        catch { return; }   // a failed read leaves the card where it was, rather than blanking it
        if (_gone || Equals(fresh, _index)) return;   // IndexProgress is a record: value equality, no needless repaint
        await InvokeAsync(() =>
        {
            _index = fresh;
            StateHasChanged();
        });
    }

    public void Dispose() => _gone = true;
}
